}
```

**Grid (also modern, clean):**
```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
}
```

**Absolute positioning (if you know the div's size):**
```css
.child {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
```

**Margin auto (horizontal only, or if you set a fixed height):**
```css
.child {
  margin: 0 auto; /* horizontal center only */
  /* or for both: */
  margin: auto;
}
```

Flexbox is the go-to for most cases. Need vertical + horizontal centering? Flexbox or Grid. Just horizontal? `margin: 0 auto` works fine.
